{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_96e26c6c38084d9599267af0762eb3a4|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2af06b087d1aca72b8674df5559","toolName":"codemode","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Script failed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"text","text":"==> text 1/4 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF-2.md\",\"value\":\"# Repair brief 2 for step build-fix-2 (supervisor, 2026-11-15)\\n\\nRead this file first, then `05-deploy/output/REVIEW-findings.md` (independent review, round 1, verdict: changes required).\\nApproved scope is unchanged: `brief.md` (issue #864). You have at most 40 responses. Do the items in order.\\n\\n## Item 1, blocking: finding I-1\\n\\nIn link mode in the repository garden, the graph is drawn at one place and hit-tested three rows lower.\\n`render` in `src/tend/mod.rs` moves the graph down only when `!tend.detail && !tend.is_linking() && tend.connection_scope()` and the summary is not empty.\\n`pointer` in the same file moves the hit rectangle down when `connection_scope()` and the summary is not empty, without the other two conditions.\\nThe supervisor confirmed both conditions in the code. The reviewer reproduced a needs link written by a click on empty space.\\n\\n- Use one condition for both paths: one small private helper that `render` and `pointer` both call. Do not copy the condition a second time.\\n- Add a terminal regression in repository scope with link mode: a click on a visible goal writes the intended needs link, and a click three rows\\n  below it writes nothing. Run it at 80×24 and 100×30 with colour off, with temporary TEST roots.\\n- Prove the regression fails when the helper is bypassed in `pointer`, then restore the source and rebuild. Record that probe.\\n- Check every other place that uses the garden body rectangle (drag, hover, release, scroll, selection) for the same mismatch, and say what you checked.\\n\\n## Item 2, small: finding N-1\\n\\nAfter `persist_noclobber` succeeds, a failed directory sync must not say \\\"Thought not saved\\\". Say that the thought is saved and that\\npersistence is uncertain, in the same manner as the correction store's message. Keep the words visible. No new mechanism.\\n\\n## Item 3, small: finding N-3\\n\\nName the thought keys in Tend's help text, where the other garden keys are explained. Do not change the garden key bar.\\nUpdate `docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md` only if the help contract is written there.\\n\\n## Not in this repair\\n\\nFinding N-2 (Ctrl+C in the reader) and the reviewer's questions Q1 and Q2 are operator decisions. Leave them as built.\\n\\n## Checks and boundaries\\n\\n- Focused: `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_repo_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`,\\n  `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, `tests/test_documentation.py`, fmt and Clippy with `-D warnings`.\\n- Full: `python3 scripts/full-check.py` from the checkout root, unchanged, with its own temporary TEST HOME in the system temporary directory.\\n  Never place TEST roots inside the checkout or in the operator HOME.\\n- Checklist marks made on the older candidate need a re-check: after the full check passes on committed work, mark again each item that this\\n  change can affect, with `sdlc.py mark`. Do not run `verify`, `step`, `stage` or `decide`.\\n- No scope beyond these items. No provider calls, no subagents. After three failed fixes of one defect, stop and report.\\n- Commit before you end. Write the report at the path in your step contract, result first, with counts.\\n\"}\n==> text 2/4 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/05-deploy/output/REVIEW-findings.md\",\"value\":\"Round: 1\\nReviewer session: 01a1de7c-36c7-7638-a5ef-fdffd6391de1\\n\\n# Review findings: issue-864-tend-thought, round 1\\n\\nCandidate: `279077f` (code at `d3e0e84`), diff `git diff 04c2bc4 HEAD -- . ':!runs'`.\\nReviewer model vendor: Anthropic (`claude-opus-5-5`). The author used a different vendor.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\n**changes required**\\n\\nOne Important finding blocks: mouse picking in link mode is now offset by three rows in the repository garden.\\nA click on a visible goal does nothing. A click on empty space three rows below a goal writes a needs link.\\nThe other Done-when lines hold on the evidence I checked. No other blocker was found.\\n\\n## Findings, by severity\\n\\n### I-1 (Important, blocks): link-mode mouse picks are offset by three rows in the repository garden\\n\\n- Location: `src/tend/mod.rs:301-310` (pointer) against `src/tend/mod.rs:467-483` (render).\\n- Observed in code: `render` draws the thought summary and moves the graph down three rows only when\\n  `!tend.detail && !tend.is_linking() && tend.connection_scope()`.\\n  `pointer` moves the hit-test rectangle down three rows when `connection_scope()` is true. It does not check `is_linking()`.\\n  In link mode, the graph is drawn at one place and hit-tested at another.\\n  `Garden::summary()` is never empty, so every repository garden with a repository is affected, also with no saved thoughts.\\n- Checked, 100×30, temporary TEST root, binary built from `279077f`, fixture from `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`:\\n  - All-goals scope (`a`, then `l`), click on the visible ring of the second goal at (73,14): `needs.json` = `{\\\"needs\\\":[{\\\"goal\\\":\\\"goal-0\\\",\\\"needs\\\":\\\"goal-1\\\"}]}`.\\n  - Repository scope (`l`), the same visible ring at (73,14): `needs.json` absent. The click did nothing.\\n  - Repository scope (`l`), the label at (64,11) and (64,8): `needs.json` absent.\\n  - Repository scope (`l`), empty space at (73,17), three rows below the ring: `needs.json` = the link above.\\n- Effect: a functional regression outside the issue's scope. A click on empty space writes a needs link that the operator did not aim at.\\n  Linking is a needs write, so this touches saved data, not only selection.\\n- Why CI did not catch it: `tests/tend_terminal.py` exercises `link-mouse` outside a repository, where `thoughts` is `None`.\\n  `tests/tend_repo_terminal.py` clicks in the repository garden only outside link mode, where render and pointer agree.\\n- Repair direction (proposal): use one condition for both paths, for example one helper that both `render` and `pointer` call.\\n  Add a repository-scope `link-mouse` regression and prove that it fails with the guard reverted.\\n- Probe scripts (outside the repository): `/tmp/review864/link_click.py`, `/tmp/review864/link_ctrl.py`.\\n\\n### N-1 (Nit, does not block): a failed directory sync reports \\\"not saved\\\" after the thought file is in place\\n\\n- Location: `src/tend/thought.rs:146-151`.\\n- Observed in code: `persist_noclobber` succeeds, then `fs::File::open(root).and_then(sync_all)` can fail.\\n  The screen then shows `Thought not saved: …` while the file exists. A second F2 shows `Thought already saved`.\\n- Not reproduced. A directory fsync failure is rare. The words are not lost, but the screen claim is false in that case.\\n\\n### N-2 (Nit, does not block): Ctrl+C does nothing while the thought editor or reader is open\\n\\n- Location: `src/menu.rs:621-631`.\\n- Observed in code: the thought block returns before the generic `Ctrl+C` quit. In the editor, `Words` treats Ctrl+C as copy.\\n  In the read-only reader, Ctrl+C is swallowed. Esc or F10 closes the view first.\\n- This matches other text editors. In the read-only reader it is a small surprise. Operator preference.\\n\\n### N-3 (Nit, does not block): Tend help does not name `t`, `v` or `g`\\n\\n- The garden key bar is unchanged by design (`docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md`). The summary line names `t` and `v`.\\n  `grep -rn thought` finds no Tend help text. The keys are discoverable only from the summary line.\\n\\n## Checked facts, by brief risk\\n\\n1. Input routing. Checked in code (`src/menu.rs:621-650`, `:437-444`, `:1090-1092`, `:1195-1201`):\\n   - `t` and `v` act only when no connection panel is open, not in detail, not linking, not in help, in repository scope,\\n     with Press and no modifiers. History requires detail (`r` acts only in detail). Tend `how` acts only under help.\\n   - While the thought view is active, it receives all keys, paste and render. Mouse input is ignored. `g` acts only inside the reader.\\n   - No other Tend mode that owns text was found. The connection-panel correction leak is repaired and covered.\\n   - The pointer path is the leak that remains (I-1). It is a mouse path, not a key path.\\n2. Authority. Checked:\\n   - Only F2 in the editor calls `save`. The editor names the repository and says \\\"No model call. No goal confirmation.\\\"\\n   - Saved JSON is `{schema, repo, words}` with `words` written unchanged. The journey checks bytes with CR, CRLF, tab, ZWJ emoji and edge spaces.\\n   - `thought.rs` imports no session, record, Shape or provider module. `g` builds a fresh `make_dump()` and pastes. `BrainDump::paste` → `Note::insert` keeps bytes.\\n   - The promotion journey shows no provider call before the operator presses F2 in Think.\\n3. \\\"Listed in the garden\\\". Count plus one summary line, full list behind `v`. See the operator questions below.\\n4. Storage. Checked in code:\\n   - The file name is `thought-<sha256(repo path)>-<sha256(words)>.json`. Read checks schema, repo, non-empty, size and the name. Duplicates are exact bytes.\\n   - `O_NOFOLLOW | O_NONBLOCK`, a regular-file check and a read cap of `LIMIT*6+4096` bytes. A temp file plus `persist_noclobber`, with file and directory fsync.\\n   - An existing different file at the same name is refused, not replaced.\\n   - A malformed or foreign file is counted as unreadable. The store error stays visible. An unwritable store refuses and keeps the editor words.\\n   - No collision: the same directory holds `needs.json`, `needs.lock` and `connection-<sha256(repo)>.json`. The `thought-` prefix is distinct.\\n   - The repository key is the raw `Repo::root()` path, the same as `connection-*.json`. It is not canonicalized.\\n   - Terminal control bytes in a saved thought do not reach the terminal.\\n     I wrote `ESC[2J`, `ESC[H` and an OSC title into a thought file. The summary showed the visible text only. The raw PTY output held no `ESC[2J`.\\n5. Promotion. Checked in the journey and code. `g` opens Think unsent, the confirmation record's first turn equals the thought bytes,\\n   and the thought file bytes are unchanged afterwards. The goal needs the existing typed `confirm`.\\n6. Tests. `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py` drives the real binary through a PTY. It reads files only as a user can see them. It adds no test-only accessor.\\n   I ran it at `279077f`: \\\"Thought journeys passed at 80x24 and 100x30 without colour. Local stubs only.\\\"\\n   I read the three probe mutations in `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`. Each one targets the named protection.\\n   The expected assertion text is distinct per probe. `probes-fix.log` records all three rejections. I did not run the probes again.\\n7. Subtraction. `src/shape/words.rs` moved to `src/words.rs` without logic change: 4 lines changed, and `pub(super)` at crate root equals crate visibility.\\n   `tests/architecture.rs` lists it as `shared`. Two features use it, so the move is justified. No code outside the issue's need was found, apart from I-1's side effect.\\n\\n## Done-when lines\\n\\n| Item | Reviewer reading |\\n|---|---|\\n| done-1 save, one disclosed action, exact bytes | Holds (journey, code). |\\n| done-2 listed after restart, labelled thought | Holds as count plus summary line. See question Q1. |\\n| done-3 no confirmation record, no Shape, not in request | Holds (journey `no_goal`, `s` check, request sources = 2). |\\n| done-4 Find connections runs with thoughts | Holds (journey with provider stub). |\\n| done-5 duplicate gives one entry and says so | Holds after restart. A duplicate in one visit was not tested, but it uses the same code path. |\\n| done-6 promotion through existing confirmation, thought stays | Holds (promotion journey). |\\n| done-7 journeys at 80×24 and 100×30, colour off | Holds for save, restart, duplicate, cancel and unwritable store. |\\n| done-8 three reversion probes | Holds on recorded evidence. I did not run it again. |\\n\\nThe release still fails on I-1. It is a regression outside the Done-when lines.\\n\\n## Hypotheses (not checked)\\n\\n- If two Tinkery processes save different words at the same moment, `create_dir_all` and `persist_noclobber` are safe. I did not run concurrent writers.\\n- A launch from a symlinked path can give a different `Repo::root()` string from a launch by the real path. Then thoughts split by path. Goals and connections share this rule.\\n\\n## Not checked\\n\\n- `python3 scripts/full-check.py`, Clippy, fmt and the full Python suite. I relied on `full-check-fix.log` for those.\\n- `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`. I did not run it again, because it rewrites source files in the checkout.\\n- Behaviour at 80×24 for I-1. I reproduced it at 100×30 only. The code path does not depend on size.\\n- Very many thought files: `read` lists the whole directory on each Tend open and each `v`. There is no count bound.\\n- Non-UTF-8 repository paths.\\n- macOS behaviour of `persist_noclobber` under a full disk.\\n\\n## Questions for the operator (product shape)\\n\\n- Q1: The issue says the thought \\\"is listed in that repository's garden\\\". The garden shows `Thoughts: N`, one first-line summary, and the full list behind `v`.\\n  Is a count plus one line enough, or must each thought show in the garden itself?\\n- Q2: Thought keys appear only in the summary line, not in the key bar or F1 help. Is that discoverable enough?\\n\\n## Skills\\n\\n`principle-prove-it-works` changed one decision. I ran the real binary in PTYs, and did not rely on code reading for I-1.\\nThat run confirmed the regression and ruled out the terminal-escape hypothesis.\\n\"}\n==> text 3/4 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff-fix.md\",\"value\":\"# Repair handoff\\n\\n## Situation\\n\\nChecked: all repair items pass on code commit `d3e0e84`.\\nThe full zero-call check passes. All eight checklist items have evidence receipts.\\nThe supervisor must run SDLC verification. Independent review and operator acceptance remain pending.\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nThe approved scope remains issue #864 in `brief.md` and `checklist.json`.\\nThis repair follows `03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md` and the `build-fix` step contract.\\nThe model pin remains `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium`.\\n\\nChanges:\\n\\n- Restored the existing garden key bars exactly. `esc back` remains visible at 80 columns.\\n- Kept thought keys in the summary. An empty thought list displays `t new thought`.\\n- Prevented thought shortcuts from taking input while the connection panel owns the screen.\\n- Replaced the broken confirmed-goal mutation with the public `shape::command::new_goal` path.\\n- Kept readable thoughts when another thought has malformed JSON or an unsupported schema.\\n- Added visible unreadable counts in the garden and reader.\\n- Added terminal regressions for the key labels and partial reads. Updated the existing design contract.\\n\\nObserved cause of the correction failure: the garden intercepted letters in `TEST corrected` while the correction editor was active.\\nThe first `t` opened the thought editor. Later input saved `ed` as a thought instead of saving the correction.\\n`correction-reproduce.log` records that screen. The repair checks that no connection panel owns the input before opening a thought.\\nThe existing correction assertion remains unchanged.\\n\\nArchitecture diagnostics 3 and 6 apply. Thought read policy stays inside `thought.rs` without changing callers.\\nThe menu owns input routing between the two panels. No new module or public interface was added.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n### Checked results\\n\\n`python3 scripts/full-check.py` passed after the code commit.\\n`full-check-fix.log` contains the complete result.\\n\\n- Rust: 1124 passed, zero failed, one ignored, across 23 reported groups.\\n- Node: 39 passed, zero failed.\\n- Python: all 86 files passed with the full tier.\\n- Formatting and workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied.\\n- Both snapshot commands and the locked build passed.\\n- `git diff --check` passed for the source repair before its commit.\\n- The evidence commit's whitespace check flags raw terminal-row padding in logs. The logs retain that output unchanged.\\n\\nAll six requested focused Python files pass in the full check.\\nSeparate checkout-local runs also passed the thought, correction, connection and documentation files.\\nThe documentation file reported 12 tests.\\n\\nThe thought file runs eight top-level journeys and 16 terminal processes across 80×24 and 100×30, with colour off.\\nIt checks save, restart, duplicate save, cancel, store refusal, repository isolation, goal promotion and partial reads.\\nSave, duplicate, cancel and refusal actions make no provider requests.\\nConnection and Think journeys use local executable stubs only.\\nSynthetic tests establish mechanics, not useful real-data connections or operator acceptance.\\n\\n### Reversion evidence\\n\\n`probes-fix.log` records all three required mutations rejected at their intended assertions:\\n\\n1. Calling `new_goal` while saving a thought fails `A thought changed goal sessions`.\\n2. Trimming saved words fails `Saved words differ from typed words`.\\n3. Adding thoughts to connection sources fails `A thought reached the provider request`.\\n\\nThe script restores sources and rebuilds the binary, then passes the clean thought journeys.\\nIt passed again after the code commit.\\n\\n`repair-reversions.log` records two additional rejected reversions.\\nRemoving the input-routing guard reproduces the correction failure.\\nRestoring fail-fast thought reading hides the valid thought and fails its restart assertion.\\nBoth sources and the binary were restored before the full check.\\n\\n### Earlier failed attempts\\n\\nTwo separate focused runs failed with TEST roots inside the checkout.\\n`goal-fix.log` shows the enclosing repository name instead of the fixture repository name.\\n`tend-fix.log` shows repository filtering where its fixture expected an outside-repository garden.\\nThese runs do not establish passing evidence.\\nBoth files subsequently passed in the unchanged full check with its permitted system-temporary TEST HOME.\\nNo unresolved test failure remains in the final full check.\\n\\n### Scope and records\\n\\nNo shared goal saver, session format, connection input or saved correction changed.\\nNo approved brief, checklist definition, factory reference or step contract changed.\\nNo named input was unreadable. No product-shape decision remains open in this repair.\\n\\n`principle-build-the-lever` changed the probe decision: the checked-in script now proves all three required faults in one command.\\n`unslop` kept the failure notices and this handoff explicit about evidence limits.\\n\\nNo production or live provider endpoint was used. Local test endpoints used synthetic fixtures.\\nNo real audio, delegation, toolchain change or Pi infrastructure edit occurred.\\nNo background job or server was left running by this repair. Terminal fixtures close their processes.\\n\\nThe generated `AGENTS.md` block, stage rules, skill snapshot and step files were already uncommitted at entry.\\nThey remain untouched and outside the repair commits.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nRun SDLC verification on the committed candidate and receipts, then obtain independent review.\\nI did not run `sdlc.py verify`, `step`, `stage` or `decide`.\\nNo PR, merge or operator acceptance is claimed.\\n\"}\n==> text 4/4 <==\n{\"path\":\"src/tend/thought.rs\",\"value\":\"//! Exact repository thoughts in Tend's private store. Thoughts never become sessions or model\\n//! sources. Only explicit saving publishes words; opening Think returns an unsent copy.\\n\\nuse crate::{Palette, words::Words};\\nuse crossterm::event::{KeyCode, KeyEvent, KeyEventKind, KeyModifiers};\\nuse ratatui::{\\n    Frame,\\n    layout::Rect,\\n    widgets::{Paragraph, Wrap},\\n};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\nuse sha2::{Digest, Sha256};\\nuse std::{\\n    fs,\\n    io::{Read, Write},\\n    os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt,\\n    path::PathBuf,\\n};\\n\\nconst LIMIT: usize = 128 * 1024;\\n\\n#[derive(Deserialize, Serialize)]\\n#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\\nstruct Thought {\\n    schema: u8,\\n    repo: PathBuf,\\n    words: String,\\n}\\n\\n/// Repository-bound words and their local editor. No goal or seed authority lives here.\\npub(crate) struct Garden {\\n    root: Result<PathBuf, String>,\\n    repo: PathBuf,\\n    entries: Result<Vec<String>, String>,\\n    unreadable: usize,\\n    selected: usize,\\n    editor: Option<Words>,\\n    viewing: bool,\\n    scroll: u16,\\n    notice: String,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Garden {\\n    /// Read only thoughts belonging to the captured launch repository; never infer attribution.\\n    pub(crate) fn open(root: Result<PathBuf, String>, repo: PathBuf) -> Self {\\n        let mut garden = Self {\\n            root,\\n            repo,\\n            entries: Ok(vec![]),\\n            unreadable: 0,\\n            selected: 0,\\n            editor: None,\\n            viewing: false,\\n            scroll: 0,\\n            notice: String::new(),\\n        };\\n        garden.entries = garden.read();\\n        garden\\n    }\\n\\n    fn prefix(&self) -> String {\\n        format!(\\n            \\\"thought-{:x}-\\\",\\n            Sha256::digest(self.repo.as_os_str().as_encoded_bytes())\\n        )\\n    }\\n\\n    fn file(&self, words: &str) -> Result<PathBuf, String> {\\n        Ok(self.root.as_ref().map_err(Clone::clone)?.join(format!(\\n            \\\"{}{:x}.json\\\",\\n            self.prefix(),\\n            Sha256::digest(words.as_bytes())\\n        )))\\n    }\\n\\n    fn read_one(&self, path: &PathBuf) -> Result<String, String> {\\n        let file = fs::OpenOptions::new()\\n            .read(true)\\n            .custom_flags(libc::O_NOFOLLOW | libc::O_NONBLOCK)\\n            .open(path)\\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        if !file.metadata().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.is_file() {\\n            return Err(\\\"A thought is not a regular local file.\\\".into());\\n        }\\n        let mut bytes = vec![];\\n        file.take((LIMIT * 6 + 4096) as u64 + 1)\\n            .read_to_end(&mut bytes)\\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        if bytes.len() > LIMIT * 6 + 4096 {\\n            return Err(\\\"A saved thought is oversized.\\\".into());\\n        }\\n        let thought: Thought = serde_json::from_slice(&bytes).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        if thought.schema != 1\\n            || thought.repo != self.repo\\n            || thought.words.is_empty()\\n            || thought.words.len() > LIMIT\\n            || self.file(&thought.words)? != *path\\n        {\\n            return Err(\\\"A thought has invalid words, repository or format.\\\".into());\\n        }\\n        Ok(thought.words)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn read(&mut self) -> Result<Vec<String>, String> {\\n        self.unreadable = 0;\\n        let root = self.root.as_ref().map_err(Clone::clone)?;\\n        let files = match fs::read_dir(root) {\\n            Ok(files) => files,\\n            Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => return Ok(vec![]),\\n            Err(e) => return Err(e.to_string()),\\n        };\\n        let mut entries = vec![];\\n        for file in files {\\n            let path = file.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\\n            if path\\n                .file_name()\\n                .is_some_and(|n| n.to_string_lossy().starts_with(&self.prefix()))\\n                && path.extension().is_some_and(|e| e == \\\"json\\\")\\n            {\\n                match self.read_one(&path) {\\n                    Ok(words) => entries.push(words),\\n                    Err(_) => self.unreadable += 1,\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        entries.sort();\\n        Ok(entries)\\n    }\\n\\n    fn save(&self, words: &str) -> Result<bool, String> {\\n        if words.is_empty() || words.len() > LIMIT {\\n            return Err(\\\"Write a thought of 1 to 131072 bytes. Nothing was saved.\\\".into());\\n        }\\n        let root = self.root.as_ref().map_err(Clone::clone)?;\\n        fs::create_dir_all(root).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        let path = self.file(words)?;\\n        let thought = Thought {\\n            schema: 1,\\n            repo: self.repo.clone(),\\n            words: words.into(),\\n        };\\n        let bytes = serde_json::to_vec(&thought).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        let mut temp = tempfile::NamedTempFile::new_in(root).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        temp.write_all(&bytes).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        temp.as_file().sync_all().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n        match temp.persist_noclobber(&path) {\\n            Ok(_) => {\\n                fs::File::open(root)\\n                    .and_then(|f| f.sync_all())\\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\\n                Ok(true)\\n            }\\n            Err(e) if e.error.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::AlreadyExists => {\\n                if self.read_one(&path)? != words {\\n                    return Err(\\\"The existing thought differs. Nothing was replaced.\\\".into());\\n                }\\n                Ok(false)\\n            }\\n            Err(e) => Err(e.to_string()),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Start a local exact-word editor. No save or provider call occurs.\\n    pub(crate) fn edit(&mut self) {\\n        self.editor = Some(Words::new(\\\"\\\"));\\n        self.notice.clear();\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Open the saved thought list without granting goal authority.\\n    pub(crate) fn view(&mut self) {\\n        self.entries = self.read();\\n        self.selected = self.selected.min(\\n            self.entries\\n                .as_ref()\\n                .map_or(0, |e| e.len().saturating_sub(1)),\\n        );\\n        self.viewing = true;\\n        self.scroll = 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Whether this local view owns keyboard and paste input.\\n    pub(crate) fn active(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.editor.is_some() || self.viewing\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Paste exact received words without saving them.\\n    pub(crate) fn paste(&mut self, text: &str) {\\n        if let Some(editor) = &mut self.editor {\\n            editor.insert(text);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Return an explicit unsent Think draft only on `g`; Shape is never a destination.\\n    pub(crate) fn key(&mut self, key: KeyEvent) -> Option<String> {\\n        if key.kind != KeyEventKind::Press {\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        if matches!(key.code, KeyCode::Esc | KeyCode::F(10)) {\\n            self.editor = None;\\n            self.viewing = false;\\n            self.notice.clear();\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        if let Some(editor) = &mut self.editor {\\n            if key.code == KeyCode::F(2) && key.modifiers == KeyModifiers::NONE {\\n                let words = editor.text().to_owned();\\n                match self.save(&words) {\\n                    Ok(created) => {\\n                        self.entries = self.read();\\n                        self.selected = self\\n                            .entries\\n                            .as_ref()\\n                            .ok()\\n                            .and_then(|entries| entries.iter().position(|w| w == &words))\\n                            .unwrap_or(0);\\n                        self.editor = None;\\n                        self.viewing = true;\\n                        self.notice = if created {\\n                            \\\"Thought saved. No goal confirmed.\\\"\\n                        } else {\\n                            \\\"Thought already saved. One entry. No goal confirmed.\\\"\\n                        }\\n                        .into();\\n                    }\\n                    Err(reason) => self.notice = format!(\\\"Thought not saved: {reason}\\\"),\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                editor.key(key);\\n            }\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        if key.modifiers != KeyModifiers::NONE {\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        let count = self.entries.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len);\\n        match key.code {\\n            KeyCode::Down | KeyCode::Char('j') => {\\n                self.selected = (self.selected + 1).min(count.saturating_sub(1));\\n                self.scroll = 0;\\n            }\\n            KeyCode::Up | KeyCode::Char('k') => {\\n                self.selected = self.selected.saturating_sub(1);\\n                self.scroll = 0;\\n            }\\n            KeyCode::PageDown => self.scroll = self.scroll.saturating_add(8),\\n            KeyCode::PageUp => self.scroll = self.scroll.saturating_sub(8),\\n            KeyCode::Char('g') => return self.entries.as_ref().ok()?.get(self.selected).cloned(),\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        None\\n    }\\n\\n    /// A labelled garden summary. Full words remain in the local read view.\\n    pub(crate) fn summary(&self) -> String {\\n        match &self.entries {\\n            Ok(entries) if self.unreadable > 0 => format!(\\n                \\\"Thoughts: {} · v read · t new thought\\\\n{} thoughts could not be read.\\\",\\n                entries.len(),\\n                self.unreadable\\n            ),\\n            Ok(entries) if entries.is_empty() => \\\"t new thought\\\".into(),\\n            Ok(entries) => format!(\\n                \\\"Thoughts: {} · v read · t new thought\\\\nThought: {}\\\",\\n                entries.len(),\\n                crate::clipped(\\n                    entries[self.selected.min(entries.len() - 1)]\\n                        .lines()\\n                        .next()\\n                        .unwrap_or(\\\"\\\"),\\n                    60\\n                )\\n            ),\\n            Err(_) => \\\"Thoughts could not be read. Press v for details. t new thought\\\".into(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Render the exact-word editor or labelled local record. Rendering reads no files.\\n    pub(crate) fn render(&mut self, frame: &mut Frame, area: Rect, palette: Palette) {\\n        let editing = self.editor.is_some();\\n        let heading = format!(\\n            \\\"{}\\\\nRepository: {}\\\\n{}{}\\\",\\n            if editing {\\n                \\\"New thought\\\"\\n            } else {\\n                \\\"Saved thoughts\\\"\\n            },\\n            self.repo.display(),\\n            if editing {\\n                \\\"F2 saves exact words here. No model call. No goal confirmation.\\\"\\n            } else {\\n                \\\"g opens these words in Think, unsent. Confirm a goal there. No Shape.\\\"\\n            },\\n            if self.unreadable > 0 {\\n                format!(\\\"\\\\n{} thoughts could not be read.\\\", self.unreadable)\\n            } else {\\n                String::new()\\n            }\\n        );\\n        let heading = Paragraph::new(heading)\\n            .style(palette.ink)\\n            .wrap(Wrap { trim: false });\\n        let rows = heading.line_count(area.width).min(area.height as usize) as u16;\\n        frame.render_widget(\\n            heading,\\n            Rect {\\n                height: rows,\\n                ..area\\n            },\\n        );\\n        let body = Rect::new(\\n            area.x,\\n            area.y.saturating_add(rows + 1),\\n            area.width,\\n            area.height.saturating_sub(rows + 4),\\n        );\\n        if let Some(editor) = &mut self.editor {\\n            editor.render(frame, body, palette, false);\\n        } else {\\n            let text = match &self.entries {\\n                Ok(entries) if entries.is_empty() => \\\"No thoughts saved.\\\".into(),\\n                Ok(entries) => format!(\\n                    \\\"Thought {} of {}\\\\n{}\\\",\\n                    self.selected + 1,\\n                    entries.len(),\\n                    entries[self.selected]\\n                        .chars()\\n                        .map(|c| if c.is_control() && c != '\\\\n' {\\n                            '�'\\n                        } else {\\n                            c\\n                        })\\n                        .collect::<String>()\\n                ),\\n                Err(reason) => format!(\\\"Thoughts could not be read: {reason}\\\"),\\n            };\\n            let p = Paragraph::new(text)\\n                .style(palette.ink)\\n                .wrap(Wrap { trim: false });\\n            self.scroll = self.scroll.min(\\n                p.line_count(body.width)\\n                    .saturating_sub(body.height as usize) as u16,\\n            );\\n            frame.render_widget(p.scroll((self.scroll, 0)), body);\\n        }\\n        frame.render_widget(\\n            Paragraph::new(self.notice.as_str())\\n                .style(palette.ink)\\n                .wrap(Wrap { trim: false }),\\n            Rect::new(area.x, area.bottom().saturating_sub(3), area.width, 2),\\n        );\\n        frame.render_widget(\\n            Paragraph::new(if editing {\\n                \\\"F2 save thought only   esc cancel\\\"\\n            } else {\\n                \\\"↑↓ thoughts   PgUp/PgDn scroll   g think   esc garden\\\"\\n            })\\n            .style(palette.muted),\\n            Rect::new(area.x, area.bottom().saturating_sub(1), area.width, 1),\\n        );\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}\nScript error:\nError: ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/tinkery/issue-864-tend-thought/tests/test_tend_thought.py'\n\nTool calls made before the