6- - Words boxes use ratatui-textarea, titled `your answer`, `your words`, `your teach-back`, `your change` or `Folder:`.\nshape-and-handoff.md-571- Configured drafting enables these actions; see [Model setup](menu.md#model-setup).\nshape-and-handoff.md-572- Shape uses Think's\nshape-and-handoff.md:573: [one key map](think.md#help): F2 runs the action in the key bar, F1 numbers the rest.\nshape-and-handoff.md-574- \nshape-and-handoff.md-575- | Stage | Words | Key/action |\nshape-and-handoff.md-593-   F2 saves them verbatim, then compares in one call behind F2's shared budget,\nshape-and-handoff.md-594-   with no tools or repository access;\nshape-and-handoff.md:595:   opening, typing, help and cancelling do not save or call. Confirmation words remain\nshape-and-handoff.md-596-   untouched. The latest completed comparison for these draft bytes appears as guesses\nshape-and-handoff.md-597-   above the risk summary; mismatches are recorded verbatim and never block confirming.\nshape-and-handoff.md-641-   the ledger; Shape adds no parallel rules. F1 lists only the actions allowed now.\nshape-and-handoff.md-642- - F2 saves exact answer bytes with `user` authority. Typing, paste, scrolling and\nshape-and-handoff.md:643:   help write nothing; held action keys never repeat. Letters, capitals and `?` remain words.\nshape-and-handoff.md-644- - The chosen harness runs one explicitly selected model with read-only tools (Pi's `read`,\nshape-and-handoff.md-645-   `grep`, `find`, `ls`; Claude Code's `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` under `dontAsk`), no commands, in the [shown folder](#grounding-in-the-repository). Input includes\nshape-and-handoff.md-809-   Confirmation words are one line, so Up and Down scroll the draft while they are typed, for\nshape-and-handoff.md-810-   terminals or multiplexers that take PgUp/PgDn (#614).\nshape-and-handoff.md:811:   Before that marker is reached, the key bar says `pgup/dn read to end` instead of\nshape-and-handoff.md-812-   offering to confirm; the confirmation hint appears on the same frame that reaches the end.\nshape-and-handoff.md:813:   Notices keep their own recovery instructions without repeating the key bar's action.\nshape-and-handoff.md-814-   The exact revision and draft bytes retain that satisfaction through typing, box growth,\nshape-and-handoff.md-815-   resize and rereads, including teach-back. A new revision or changed bytes require reading again.\nshape-and-handoff.md-924- ### Without a screen\nshape-and-handoff.md-925- \nshape-and-handoff.md:926: A key bar is friction for an agent or a script (#845: a driving agent spent 27 and 48 responses\nshape-and-handoff.md-927- pressing keys). The same ledger and step run from commands. Options go before `seed`:\nshape-and-handoff.md-928- \n==> text 6/7 <==\narchitecture.md-119- [typed history](https://github.com/jon-devlapaz/tinkery/pull/462).\narchitecture.md-120- For Shape's typed context, read [Think history](shape-and-handoff.md#think-history).\narchitecture.md-121- \narchitecture.md:122: ## Design score\narchitecture.md-123- \narchitecture.md-124- John Ousterhout's *A Philosophy of Software Design* supplies these eight questions.\narchitecture.md-125- Structural PRs name the rows they move.\n==> text 7/7 <==\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Prove thought protections by introducing three faults, then restore sources and binary.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/'tests'))\nimport test_launch\n\nTHOUGHT = ROOT/'src/tend/thought.rs'\nCONNECTION = ROOT/'src/tend/connection.rs'\nFAULTS = [\n    ('confirmed-goal', THOUGHT, '        let path = self.file(words)?;', '''        crate::shape::command::new_goal(\n            root.parent().unwrap().join(\"sessions\"),\n            words,\n            \"TEST faulty thought confirmation\",\n            &crate::think_record::GoalConfirmation::terminal(Some(\"agent\"))?,\n        )?;\n        let path = self.file(words)?;''', 'A thought changed goal sessions'),\n    ('changed-words', THOUGHT, '            words: words.into(),',\n     '            words: words.trim().into(),', 'Saved words differ from typed words'),\n    ('provider-source', CONNECTION, '        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));', '''        for entry in fs::read_dir(&self.store).map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\n            let path = entry.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\n            if path.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().starts_with(\"thought-\") {\n                let thought: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(path).unwrap()).unwrap();\n                if thought[\"repo\"] == serde_json::json!(self.repo) {\n                    sources.push(Source { id: \"TEST-thought\".into(),\n                        goal: thought[\"words\"].as_str().unwrap().into(), repo: self.repo.clone(),\n                        status: \"active\".into() });\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));''', 'A thought reached the provider request'),\n]\n\n\ndef main():\n    env = test_launch.environment()\n    output = ROOT/'target/thought-probes'\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    originals = {p: p.read_text() for p in [THOUGHT, CONNECTION]}\n\n    def build():\n        test_launch.run(['cargo', '+stable', 'build', '--locked', '--quiet'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\n\n    try:\n        for name, path, old, new, expected in FAULTS:\n            source = originals[path]\n            if source.count(old) != 1:\n                raise SystemExit(f'{name}: mutation no longer matches exactly once')\n            path.write_text(source.replace(old, new))\n            try:\n                build()\n                result = test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env,\n                                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\n                log = result.stdout + result.stderr\n                (output/f'{name}.log').write_text(log)\n                if result.returncode == 0 or expected not in log:\n                    raise SystemExit(f'{name}: protection did not fail for the expected reason\\n{log}')\n                print(f'{name}: rejected ({expected})', flush=True)\n            finally:\n                path.write_text(source)\n    finally:\n        for path, source in originals.items():\n            path.write_text(source)\n        build()\n    test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n\n[Full output: /var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-d858f2e1f68784c2.txt (read with offset/limit)]"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_a04c3f9cc2014ef3a9c4d939cfd4799a|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2b924a887d1aae86a80c9342ae4/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"tests/tend_connection_terminal.py\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":150}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5774170000004233},{"id":"call_a04c3f9cc2014ef3a9c4d939cfd4799a|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2b924a887d1aae86a80c9342ae4/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"tests/tend_thought_terminal.py\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":95}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.373249999996915},{"id":"call_a04c3f9cc2014ef3a9c4d939cfd4799a|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2b924a887d1aae86a80c9342ae4/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"src/tend/graph.rs\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.437207999995735},{"id":"call_a04c3f9cc2014ef3a9c4d939cfd4799a|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2b924a887d1aae86a80c9342ae4/4","name":"grep","args":"{\"pattern\":\"sync_all|uncertain\",\"path\":\"src\",\"context\":3,\"limit\":35}","status":"ok","durationMs":13.603792000001704},{"id":"call_a04c3f9cc2014ef3a9c4d939cfd4799a|ctc_0e8cd1afdc37c664016af9d2b924a887d1aae86a80c9342ae4/5","name":"grep","args":"{\"pattern\":\"thought|help|key bar\",\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"context\":2}","status":"ok","durationMs":6.264707999995153},{"id":"call_a04c3f